WEBVTT

00:00:02.120 --> 00:00:05.090
<b>Little time remains in the official 15-minute qualifier.</b>

00:00:05.090 --> 00:00:07.330
<b>All cars are now on their last attack.</b>

00:00:09.470 --> 00:00:13.060
<b>Currently at the top is car #7, Ishihara from Sam's.</b>

00:00:13.060 --> 00:00:15.500
<b>His time is 1 minute 43.442 seconds.</b>

00:00:15.900 --> 00:00:20.960
<b>Also from Sam's, Shiba follows in 2nd place with 1 minute 43.628 seconds.</b>

00:00:27.520 --> 00:00:28.950
<i>Taira.</i>

00:00:28.950 --> 00:00:32.270
<i>Did he lose his motivation when he heard Minamoto wasn't competing?</i>

00:00:32.820 --> 00:00:34.730
<i>Then stay where you are.</i>

00:00:35.110 --> 00:00:36.870
<i>I'm going ahead!</i>

00:00:40.070 --> 00:00:43.990
<i>I'll catch up to Minamoto before you, no matter what!</i>

00:00:44.670 --> 00:00:48.880
<i>I'll get pole position in this qualifier and accomplish a pole-to-win tomorrow.</i>

00:00:48.880 --> 00:00:51.770
<i>I'll get continuous wins in place of Minamoto!</i>

00:00:53.580 --> 00:00:55.410
<b>Whoa!  Shiba gets top time!</b>

00:00:55.410 --> 00:00:57.630
<b>1 minute 43.313 seconds!</b>

00:00:59.130 --> 00:01:01.310
<b>But Ishihara quickly takes it back!</b>

00:01:01.310 --> 00:01:04.020
<b>1 minute 43.208 seconds!</b>

00:01:05.550 --> 00:01:10.510
<b>Although it was announced that Minamoto Naomi isn't competing, there is no change in the strength of Sam's.</b>

00:01:10.510 --> 00:01:12.220
<b>Ishihara and Shiba.</b>

00:01:12.220 --> 00:01:17.130
<b>The team battle for pole position is heating up!</b>

00:01:22.730 --> 00:01:24.490
Don't lose, Ryou!

00:01:24.490 --> 00:01:27.710
If you win here, a chance will open up for you, too!

00:01:27.710 --> 00:01:29.910
It's a chance, Ryou!

00:01:30.830 --> 00:01:31.770
That's right.

00:01:31.770 --> 00:01:33.870
This is also a chance for Capeta.

00:01:33.870 --> 00:01:34.930
Huh?

00:01:34.930 --> 00:01:36.870
Because Minamoto-kun isn't here?

00:01:37.310 --> 00:01:42.590
Minamoto continued to win in the FSte and showed his strength.  That's why he was called to Italy.

00:01:42.590 --> 00:01:45.170
In other words, this race is the gateway to the world...

00:01:45.170 --> 00:01:47.550
It's connected all the way up to the F1!

00:03:29.670 --> 00:03:31.200
There are three minutes left.

00:03:32.280 --> 00:03:34.390
If you get out there right now,
you can do one more attack.

00:03:34.390 --> 00:03:34.820
Go!

00:03:34.820 --> 00:03:36.720
Three more minutes...

00:03:37.830 --> 00:03:38.720
That's right!

00:03:38.720 --> 00:03:40.600
The qualifier isn't finished yet!

00:03:41.930 --> 00:03:43.400
<i>What am I doing?!</i>

00:03:43.400 --> 00:03:45.290
<i>I have to do my race!</i>

00:03:45.710 --> 00:03:49.880
<i>My job is to finish the race, stand out, and leave results!</i>

00:03:49.880 --> 00:03:51.880
<i>Isn't that right... Nobu?!</i>

00:03:51.880 --> 00:03:53.010
<i>Isn't that right... Nobu?!</i>

00:03:53.010 --> 00:03:54.460
Komazawa is...

00:03:54.460 --> 00:03:57.720
He passed all sectors with top times and is now on the final corner!

00:03:57.720 --> 00:03:58.930
What?!

00:04:02.140 --> 00:04:03.650
<i>I'll do it.</i>

00:04:03.650 --> 00:04:06.610
<i>I'll show them all how fast I am!</i>

00:04:07.000 --> 00:04:09.610
<i>My fighting spirit won't lose to anyone!</i>

00:04:11.280 --> 00:04:11.700
<b>It's out!</b>

00:04:11.700 --> 00:04:13.030
<b>Persec, Komazawa.</b>

00:04:13.030 --> 00:04:15.410
<b>1 minute 42.943 seconds!</b>

00:04:15.410 --> 00:04:17.520
That's incredible!  It's the top time!

00:04:17.520 --> 00:04:19.940
He passed Ishihara and Shiba in one go!

00:04:19.940 --> 00:04:23.250
He's only 4/100ths of a second behind Minamoto's time.

00:04:23.250 --> 00:04:26.790
To think that he'd get a super lap like that...

00:04:36.780 --> 00:04:37.850
<b>Oh no!</b>

00:04:37.850 --> 00:04:40.400
<b>A car has gone out of the course at the 1st corner!</b>

00:04:40.400 --> 00:04:42.770
<b>It's Komazawa, who just got the top time!</b>

00:04:45.780 --> 00:04:46.770
Komazawa!

00:04:47.150 --> 00:04:48.060
Komazawa!  Komazawa!

00:04:48.060 --> 00:04:48.940
Komazawa!  Komazawa!

00:04:48.940 --> 00:04:50.750
<b>That was a violent crash!</b>

00:04:50.750 --> 00:04:52.610
<b>Is the driver okay?!</b>

00:05:01.820 --> 00:05:03.970
The session is now canceled.

00:05:03.970 --> 00:05:06.120
It was a violent crash.

00:05:06.600 --> 00:05:08.060
Do you think he's okay?

00:05:08.060 --> 00:05:10.340
He's Capeta's teammate, right?

00:05:10.880 --> 00:05:16.300
It looks like the machine broke well and absorbed the impact, so he's probably okay.

00:05:16.680 --> 00:05:18.990
The machine broke well?

00:05:18.990 --> 00:05:20.560
It's in pieces...

00:05:20.560 --> 00:05:24.020
How much is it going to cost to repair all that?!

00:05:40.180 --> 00:05:42.870
Like I said to them, there's nothing wrong with me!

00:05:42.870 --> 00:05:45.120
And they went on about the rules and stuff.

00:05:46.580 --> 00:05:47.830
Komazawa-san!

00:05:47.830 --> 00:05:49.500
Are you okay?

00:05:49.500 --> 00:05:51.430
Of course!

00:05:51.430 --> 00:05:54.360
There's nothing wrong with me, but those marshals were pushy.

00:05:54.360 --> 00:05:55.270
You idiot!

00:05:55.270 --> 00:05:56.880
We were worried!

00:05:56.880 --> 00:05:59.140
That's great, Komazawa!

00:05:59.660 --> 00:06:01.500
In any case, it's a relief.

00:06:01.500 --> 00:06:04.720
The doctor said you didn't injure yourself.

00:06:04.720 --> 00:06:07.980
Like I'd get injured in a crash like that!

00:06:07.980 --> 00:06:09.730
I'm an invincible man!

00:06:11.340 --> 00:06:14.190
If you had injured yourself after getting the pole...

00:06:14.900 --> 00:06:16.210
Pole?  Me?

00:06:16.210 --> 00:06:17.030
Pole?  Me?

00:06:17.030 --> 00:06:20.150
Yup, 1 minute 42.943 seconds.

00:06:20.150 --> 00:06:21.280
It's an amazing time record!

00:06:21.830 --> 00:06:27.150
It's only you and Minamoto who have driven within the 42-second range on this circuit, after all.

00:06:28.660 --> 00:06:31.290
Well, this is what I get if I do it seriously.

00:06:31.290 --> 00:06:32.830
What are you talking about?

00:06:32.830 --> 00:06:34.460
You made us all worry.

00:06:34.460 --> 00:06:36.120
You!  You!

00:06:36.120 --> 00:06:37.670
Yo!  Genius Driver!

00:06:37.670 --> 00:06:39.470
The invincible man!

00:06:39.470 --> 00:06:41.320
That's our ace!  Just as expected!

00:06:41.320 --> 00:06:44.030
<i>Komazawa-san did his best and got a result.</i>

00:06:45.290 --> 00:06:46.870
<i>But...  I...</i>

00:06:46.870 --> 00:06:47.980
<i>But...  I...</i>

00:06:50.990 --> 00:06:53.400
It's great you got the pole, but...

00:06:53.400 --> 00:06:56.650
we won't be able to use this in tomorrow's race.

00:07:02.850 --> 00:07:04.250
That's okay!

00:07:04.250 --> 00:07:06.150
We still have the spare car!

00:07:06.150 --> 00:07:08.790
We brought three cars,
 so even if we can't use this one...

00:07:08.790 --> 00:07:10.050
That's right.

00:07:10.050 --> 00:07:12.040
It's also his chance for a first win.

00:07:12.040 --> 00:07:13.470
Win?

00:07:13.470 --> 00:07:16.760
You think we could aim for the win in a car that hasn't been tuned up?

00:07:21.550 --> 00:07:26.510
This car was tuned up with the best engine and frame.

00:07:27.010 --> 00:07:31.640
Although the third car is a spare,
 it's secondhand and used as a practice car.

00:07:31.640 --> 00:07:34.800
If you drove it normally, it'd be 0.5 seconds slower.

00:07:34.800 --> 00:07:39.940
If you went out in the final with that,
you wouldn't be able to fight with the top cars.

00:07:39.940 --> 00:07:41.260
I'll do something about it!

00:07:41.260 --> 00:07:42.640
Leave it to me!

00:07:42.640 --> 00:07:44.310
It doesn't matter if it's a practice car.

00:07:44.310 --> 00:07:45.530
Let me drive!

00:07:48.490 --> 00:07:50.830
Please, Tsubomaki-san!

00:08:02.150 --> 00:08:03.050
Taira.

00:08:03.050 --> 00:08:05.510
Hand over your car to Komazawa.

00:08:08.220 --> 00:08:10.820
The race is all about results.

00:08:10.820 --> 00:08:13.860
Komazawa got the top time and is in pole position.

00:08:13.860 --> 00:08:17.410
As a team, the obvious thing to do is to give priority to the one who got results.

00:08:19.360 --> 00:08:21.940
Komazawa is our ace.

00:08:22.390 --> 00:08:25.550
The ace has the right to choose the fastest car.

00:08:25.550 --> 00:08:29.910
And with that car, we're going to get Komazawa to win this race!

00:08:29.910 --> 00:08:32.120
But then Capeta is...!

00:08:32.490 --> 00:08:35.580
The job of the second driver is to support the ace.

00:08:35.950 --> 00:08:39.090
For that, he wouldn't have trouble in the spare car.

00:08:43.620 --> 00:08:44.430
But...

00:08:46.100 --> 00:08:49.430
In its current state, there's not enough fighting strength in that spare car.

00:08:49.780 --> 00:08:53.390
Out of the engines we brought, this one is working the best.

00:08:53.840 --> 00:08:57.860
After making a check, if there's nothing wrong with it, we'll switch this engine over to the spare car.

00:09:01.000 --> 00:09:02.050
All right?

00:09:02.050 --> 00:09:03.020
Yes!

00:09:13.840 --> 00:09:15.770
Okay, it's running fine.

00:09:15.770 --> 00:09:17.500
We can somehow manage with this.

00:09:19.880 --> 00:09:20.840
I'm sorry.

00:09:23.090 --> 00:09:24.250
What are you doing?

00:09:24.800 --> 00:09:27.220
I thought that maybe I could help out with something.

00:09:27.750 --> 00:09:29.260
You can go.

00:09:29.840 --> 00:09:30.720
But...

00:09:31.710 --> 00:09:33.900
Your job is to drive.

00:09:33.900 --> 00:09:35.730
Sleep well and get ready for tomorrow.

00:09:37.340 --> 00:09:39.920
Leave the car to us.

00:09:46.810 --> 00:09:49.720
My job is to drive... huh.

00:09:49.720 --> 00:09:50.640
My job is to drive... huh.

00:09:51.370 --> 00:09:53.390
<i>Your job is to drive, right?</i>

00:09:53.390 --> 00:09:57.470
<i>In order to drive your best tomorrow, it's your job now to rest.</i>

00:10:06.340 --> 00:10:07.770
Let's go, Sarukkii.

00:10:07.770 --> 00:10:10.270
I have to sleep well for tomorrow.

00:10:20.310 --> 00:10:22.820
<i>It's not like I took it away from him by force.</i>

00:10:22.820 --> 00:10:27.610
<i>Tsubomaki-san even said that the ace has the right to ride the fastest car.</i>

00:10:28.370 --> 00:10:30.070
<i>Hand over your car to Komazawa.</i>

00:10:35.230 --> 00:10:37.130
<i>I won't let anyone complain.</i>

00:10:37.770 --> 00:10:39.380
<i>The race is all about results.</i>

00:10:41.270 --> 00:10:42.680
<i>I just need to win!</i>

00:10:49.540 --> 00:10:52.400
<i>It's been 6 years since he started driving the kart.</i>

00:10:52.950 --> 00:10:57.730
<i>There were a lot of sad times and tough times, but we finally got this far.</i>

00:10:58.410 --> 00:11:02.190
<i>The formula car that leads to the F1.  The first step.</i>

00:11:02.190 --> 00:11:05.680
<i>He's finally going to step forward today.</i>

00:11:07.830 --> 00:11:09.320
You're up early, Nobu-kun.

00:11:09.720 --> 00:11:12.770
Uncle, we need to hurry up; eat and get ready.

00:11:12.770 --> 00:11:14.530
Capeta is waiting at the circuit.

00:11:14.530 --> 00:11:15.760
Yeah.

00:11:15.760 --> 00:11:17.040
You're right.

00:11:30.270 --> 00:11:34.110
Other than the engine, we haven't gotten everything adjusted.

00:11:34.110 --> 00:11:37.140
We have no choice but to set it up during the free practice, but...

00:11:37.650 --> 00:11:39.650
there's no guarantee that it'll run properly.

00:11:39.650 --> 00:11:40.860
That's okay.

00:11:40.860 --> 00:11:42.100
I'll make it run.

00:11:43.830 --> 00:11:44.620
Yeah.

00:11:46.510 --> 00:11:47.830
Hey, how's it looking?

00:11:47.830 --> 00:11:51.490
We'll have to run it and re-adjust.

00:11:52.520 --> 00:11:53.790
Are you... sure it's okay?

00:11:53.790 --> 00:11:54.950
Are you... sure it's okay?

00:11:55.470 --> 00:11:56.200
Yeah.

00:11:57.130 --> 00:12:02.800
This is the machine that the team set up for me overnight.  My machine.

